    "S1": {
      "headline": "Paid hours look vulnerable before job titles change.",
      "whatTheyDo": [
        {
          "tag": "change-job",
          "text": "147 include **finding or changing work**, often after an hours cut and subject to a real paid offer."
        },
        {
          "tag": "learn-ai",
          "text": "143 include **learning AI tools**, with paid practice and measured checking recurring in the plans."
        },
        {
          "tag": "keep-going",
          "text": "91 include **continuing current work**, including paid fallback duties when another plan is unavailable."
        },
        {
          "tag": "collective-action",
          "text": "69 include **union or association action** about paid hours, error evidence or redeployment."
        }
      ],
      "whatTheySay": [
        "Public requests focus on **measured errors**, named responsibility and paid time before targets change.",
        "Some seek **staff representation** before fewer people are asked to cover more files."
      ],
      "whatTheyThink": [
        "**Own paid hours** can shrink even when an experienced reviewer or tool operator expects to stay.",
        "**Household buffers** buy time, while partner wages often cannot replace the lost accounting income."
      ],
      "howTheyFeel": [
        "**153 are anxious** and 25 alarmed; 23 are calm or uneasy, with none panicked.",
        "The **3.00 average worry** reflects own income exposure, beyond discomfort with unfamiliar software."
      ],
      "segments": {
        "least": {
          "name": "Less immediate danger",
          "story": "Three calm and 20 uneasy profiles form the calmer end; 14 of these 23 have strong cushions."
        },
        "most": {
          "name": "Expected income cuts",
          "story": "25 profiles are alarmed, including 23 with thin cushions; none is panicked in this scenario."
        }
      },
      "differences": [
        {
          "group": "Money cushion",
          "text": "Mean worry is **3.28 for thin cushions** (72 profiles), versus 2.75 for strong cushions (63)."
        },
        {
          "group": "Adaptability",
          "text": "Mean worry is **3.19 for resistant profiles**, versus 2.76 for adaptive profiles (67 in each group)."
        }
      ],
      "quotes": [
        {
          "id": "A21-13113",
          "name": "Lena Costa",
          "text": "I want our staff association at the meeting where partners decide which accounting jobs disappear."
        },
        {
          "id": "A21-23222",
          "name": "Bianca Dubois",
          "text": "The reserve buys time to look, not permission to ignore the payslip."
        }
      ],
